  ],
  "method": "Bring the milk just to a boil, then simmer 5 minutes to concentrate it\nslightly — this gives a thicker set. Cool to 40–43°C: the milk should feel\ndistinctly warm, not hot, on a clean fingertip held for ten seconds. Whisk\nthe starter curd until smooth, stir it through the milk, cover, and leave\ncompletely undisturbed for 6 to 8 hours at around 30°C. In cold weather, set\nthe pot inside a switched-off oven with the light on, or wrap it in a thick\ntowel next to a hot-water bottle. The curd is set when it jiggles as one mass\nand the surface releases a little clear whey. Refrigerate immediately once\nset; over-fermenting at room temperature turns it sharply sour by evening.\nSave 30g as the starter for tomorrow's batch."
}

